course: dictionary
lesson: 11674
title: Assisted: helped along
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Assisted is the past form of the verb assist, and it means helped. «She assisted the teacher with the paints.» The teacher was given help, so assisted means helped.
explain: In sport, assist has a special meaning. «He scored two goals and assisted one.» Here it means he passed the ball to a player who then scored, so he helped that goal happen.
explain: Assisted can also describe something done with help. «Power-assisted steering» makes turning the wheel easier, and «assisted living» means homes where older people get daily help. Ask yourself: who is helping, and with what?
fact: Assist means to help, and assisted is its past form.
fact: «Assisted» means helped: «she assisted the teacher» means she helped the teacher.
fact: In football, hockey and basketball, to assist means to pass the ball to a player who then scores.
fact: «Assisted living» means homes where older people get help every day.
fact: The other forms of the verb are assist, assists and assisting.
exercise: «The helper assisted the teacher with the books.» What does assisted mean? | Forgot | Hurt | Shouted at | *Helped
exercise: «He scored two goals and assisted one.» In football, what does assisted mean here? | Stopped a goal from going in | Watched from the bench | *Passed the ball to a player who scored | Kicked the ball out of play
exercise: «Grandma lives in assisted living, where staff help her every day.» What is assisted living? | *Homes where older people get daily help | Schools for young athletes | Houses with no doors at all | Shops that sell steering wheels
test: «Dad assisted me with my maths homework.» What does assisted mean? | *Helped | Copied | Worried | Stopped
test: «The car has power-assisted steering, so turning the wheel is easy.» What does power-assisted mean? | *Steering that uses a motor to help the driver | Steering only for boats | Steering with no engine at all | Steering that is very hard to turn
exam: What does assisted mean in «The volunteers assisted the families after the flood»? | Left | *Helped | Sold | Ignored
